title: Point-and-click adventures
intro: Click somewhere and the player walks there, round whatever's in the way; click a hotspot and it walks over to look at it or use it. No code.
project: Empty | Adventure

chapter: A floor to walk on | Walk areas and a walker
# Built from Empty and Sprite, a component at a time (Entity > Genres > Adventures > Walk Area, Hotspot and Walker make the same in
# one go).
create: Empty
rename: Floor
set: Transform.Position = 0, -2, 0
add: WalkArea
expectcomponents: Floor = Transform, WalkArea
explain: component:WalkArea | A walk area | A walk area is a shape round the floor of a room, where the player can walk. The Scene view draws it in blue.
explain: handle:WalkArea.2 | A corner | Drag its corners to fit the room, or a plus to add one; each change is one undo step.
path: WalkArea.2 = 6, -1.5
path: WalkArea.3 = 5, 1.5
expectvalue: Floor.WalkArea.Points = -4 -1.5; 6 -1.5; 5 1.5; -4 1.5
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Player
set: Transform.Position = -3, -1.4, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.8, 1.6
set: Sprite.Tint = #4C8DF0
set: Sprite.Order = 10
add: Walker
explain: component:Walker | A walker | A walker is the player: it walks wherever the floor is clicked, on its feet, the bottom of its sprite.
deselect
create: Empty
rename: Table
set: Transform.Position = 0, -2, 0
add: WalkArea
set: WalkArea.Blocks = true
set: WalkArea.Points = -1 -0.7; 1 -0.7; 1 0.7; -1 0.7
add: Sprite
set: Sprite.Size = 2, 1.4
set: Sprite.Tint = #8A5A33
explain: field:WalkArea.Blocks | A hole | Ticking Blocks makes a hole in the floor where nobody walks: a table in the middle of the room.
deselect
play
wait: 0.5
gameclick: 3.5, -2.2
wait: 2.5
expectat: Player = 3.5, -1.4
explain: game | Round the table | A click on the floor walks the player there, round the table, along the shortest way, facing the way it goes.
gameclick: -3, -3
wait: 2.5
expectat: Player = -3, -2.2
stop

chapter: Something to look at | Hotspots
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Bell
set: Transform.Position = 4.5, 2, 0
add: Hotspot
set: Hotspot.Name = Brass Bell
set: Hotspot.Points = -0.5 -0.5; 0.5 -0.5; 0.5 0.5; -0.5 0.5
set: Hotspot.StandAt = 0, -4
set: Hotspot.LookLine = A brass bell, thick with dust.
set: Hotspot.UseLine = Ding!
set: Hotspot.UseFlag = RangBell
set: Sprite.Size = 0.8, 0.8
set: Sprite.Tint = #E8C54A
explain: component:Hotspot | A hotspot | A hotspot is something to look at and use: a line for each, and an action, a flag or a message too. Stand At is where the player stands to do it.
deselect
play
wait: 0.5
gamehover: Bell
wait: 0.5
explain: game | Its name | Over a hotspot the pointer shows its name and turns into a hand.
gameorder: Bell
wait: 2.5
expectvalue: Player.Walker.Said = A brass bell, thick with dust.
explain: game | Looked at | A right click walks over and looks at it: the player says its line.
gameclick: Bell
wait: 1.2
expectvalue: Player.Walker.Said = Ding!
expectvalue: Bell.Hotspot.TimesUsed = 1
explain: game | Used | A left click uses it, setting its flag as well.
stop

chapter: Someone to talk to | Using a character starts its dialogue
deselect
create: Dialogue Box
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Guard
set: Transform.Position = -4.5, -0.5, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.8, 1.6
set: Sprite.Tint = #57AB5A
add: Hotspot
set: Hotspot.StandAt = 1.5, -1.5
set: Hotspot.UseTalks = true
add: Dialogue
set: Dialogue.Lines = Halt! Who rang that bell?\nKeep it down, will you?
explain: field:Hotspot.UseTalks | Talking | Use Talks starts the dialogue on the hotspot's entity, so a character is a hotspot with something to say.
deselect
play
wait: 0.5
gameclick: Guard
wait: 2.5
expectvalue: Dialogue Box.Text.Value = Halt! Who rang that bell?
explain: game | Clicks move it on | Clicks and taps move the talk on, so the whole game plays with the mouse or on a touch screen.
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 1
expectvalue: Dialogue Box.Text.Value = Keep it down, will you?
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 1
expectat: Player = -3, -1.2
stop

chapter: Further away | Depth
select: Floor
set: WalkArea.FarScale = 0.6
explain: field:WalkArea.FarScale | Far Scale | Far Scale shrinks walkers towards the top of the floor, as if further away, and they walk slower there too.
deselect
play
wait: 0.5
gameclick: 4, 1
wait: 3
expectat: Player = 4, 0.25
explain: game | Smaller | At the back of the room the player is drawn smaller.
stop
